WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:15.311
stared at Cole in shock.

2
00:00:16.112 --> 00:00:17.073
So did everyone else.

3
00:00:17.093 --> 00:00:22.277
"Your flip-flops were at the scene of the crime," Kyle said, pointing at Cole.

4
00:00:22.297 --> 00:00:25.680
"That means you dumped the frogs back in the water!"

5
00:00:26.621 --> 00:00:27.341
John nodded.

6
00:00:27.361 --> 00:00:30.164
"I bet he did it the first time too."

7
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.180
"I knew it!"

8
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.321
Lauren muttered.

9
00:00:34.721 --> 00:00:36.041
Henry didn't know what to think.

10
00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:38.662
Those flip-flops were a big clue.

11
00:00:39.662 --> 00:00:40.943
Could Cole be the culprit?

12
00:00:41.843 --> 00:00:43.744
After all, Cole did love a good joke.

13
00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:47.985
But Cole was shaking his head, looking more upset than ever.

14
00:00:48.005 --> 00:00:49.865
"I didn't do it!"

15
00:00:50.185 --> 00:00:51.266
he told Coach Phillips.

16
00:00:52.286 --> 00:00:52.846
"I swear!"

17
00:00:52.866 --> 00:00:55.907
That brought Henry back to his senses.

18
00:00:56.847 --> 00:00:59.308
Cole might be a joker, but he wasn't a liar.

19
00:01:00.756 --> 00:01:03.277
If Cole said he was innocent, then Henry believed him.

20
00:01:04.378 --> 00:01:06.238
But he could tell most of the others didn't.

21
00:01:07.199 --> 00:01:09.620
Even Coach Phillips had a doubtful frown on his face.

22
00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.881
"We'll talk about it later," the coach said.

23
00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:16.142
"First we'd better get those frogs rounded up again."

24
00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:20.784
The swimmers all jumped in the pool and started catching frogs.

25
00:01:21.865 --> 00:01:23.045
Henry and Maggie watched.

26
00:01:23.065 --> 00:01:26.887
"This doesn't look good for Cole," Maggie whispered.

27
00:01:26.907 --> 00:01:30.068
"I know," Henry whispered back.

28
00:01:31.252 --> 00:01:35.413
"If we don't solve this mystery fast, Cole will never make the swim team!"

29
00:01:37.014 --> 00:01:41.995
"Someone must have put Cole's flip-flops by the buckets so he'd get the blame," Maggie said.

30
00:01:42.015 --> 00:01:44.096
"Who could have done that?"

31
00:01:44.116 --> 00:01:46.036
"I don't know."

32
00:01:47.137 --> 00:01:51.138
Henry tried to remember who had been near the pool when he and Maggie had returned.

33
00:01:52.198 --> 00:01:53.499
The coach had been there of course.

34
00:01:54.479 --> 00:01:57.280
So had a few of the faster joggers, including Cole.

35
00:01:58.508 --> 00:02:01.089
But Henry couldn't remember who else was in the fast group.

36
00:02:02.629 --> 00:02:04.050
Maggie was staring at Lauren.

37
00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:08.011
The assistant coach was watching the swimmers retrieve the frogs.

38
00:02:09.191 --> 00:02:12.372
"Lauren was the one who spotted the flip-flops," Maggie said.

39
00:02:12.392 --> 00:02:15.573
"Maybe that's because she was the one who put them there."

40
00:02:15.593 --> 00:02:18.254
"Maybe," Henry agreed.

41
00:02:19.114 --> 00:02:20.114
"Let's go talk to her.

42
00:02:21.254 --> 00:02:23.615
But let me ask most of the questions, okay?

43
00:02:24.555 --> 00:02:26.396
We don't want her to know we're suspicious of her."

44
00:02:27.468 --> 00:02:28.249
Maggie frowned.

45
00:02:29.069 --> 00:02:29.750
But she nodded.

46
00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:32.352
"Okay," she said.

47
00:02:35.474 --> 00:02:36.615
They walked over to Lauren.

48
00:02:36.635 --> 00:02:38.816
"Hi," Henry said.

49
00:02:38.836 --> 00:02:42.099
"I'm Henry, and this is my cousin Maggie."

50
00:02:42.119 --> 00:02:44.360
"Nice to meet you.

51
00:02:45.321 --> 00:02:46.862
I'm Lauren," Lauren said.

52
00:02:46.882 --> 00:02:49.404
"Are you here to try out for the team?

53
00:02:50.545 --> 00:02:53.167
Because we usually recommend wearing a swimsuit."

54
00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:54.908
Henry laughed.

55
00:02:55.988 --> 00:02:59.110
"No, we're just here to watch our friends try out."

56
00:03:00.151 --> 00:03:02.492
"You didn't bring your pet frogs with you, did you?"

57
00:03:02.892 --> 00:03:04.653
Lauren asked, smiling a little.

58
00:03:06.234 --> 00:03:09.916
Henry's dad was a reporter who had a lot of experience interviewing people.

59
00:03:11.077 --> 00:03:16.460
Henry suddenly remembered his dad's advice: A good way to start an interview is to ask people about

60
00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:21.883
themselves. "We heard you're a student at Bellville College," Henry said to Lauren.

61
00:03:21.903 --> 00:03:23.504
"Do you like it there?"

62
00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:27.021
"Sure, it's great," Lauren said.

63
00:03:27.041 --> 00:03:29.341
"I've been there for three years.

64
00:03:30.282 --> 00:03:31.582
I'll graduate next spring."

65
00:03:31.602 --> 00:03:34.423
"Really?" Maggie blurted out.

66
00:03:34.443 --> 00:03:37.724
"Wow, you look much younger than that!"

67
00:03:39.684 --> 00:03:42.485
Lauren's friendly expression instantly changed to a frown.

68
00:03:42.505 --> 00:03:45.646
"Excuse me," she snapped.

69
00:03:45.666 --> 00:03:47.587
"I have work to do."

70
00:03:49.687 --> 00:03:51.608
Henry sighed as Lauren stomped away.

71
00:03:53.525 --> 00:03:57.868
"You already knew she was sensitive about looking young," he said to Maggie.

72
00:03:57.888 --> 00:04:00.530
"Why did you have to mention it?"

73
00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:03.732
"Sorry." Maggie shrugged.

74
00:04:04.652 --> 00:04:05.613
"I couldn't help it."

75
00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:08.895
Henry knew better than to get annoyed at his cousin.

76
00:04:10.397 --> 00:04:14.319
She had a habit of saying whatever was on her mind without thinking about it first.

77
00:04:14.339 --> 00:04:18.302
"Forget about it," he murmured, thinking hard.

78
00:04:19.383 --> 00:04:20.464
Maggie was thinking too.

79
00:04:21.484 --> 00:04:23.785
"Lauren is so sensitive about her age.

80
00:04:24.765 --> 00:04:26.666
She's probably still mad at Cole.

81
00:04:28.147 --> 00:04:31.108
Maybe even mad enough to try to get him kicked out of tryouts!"

82
00:04:32.349 --> 00:04:33.789
"Right," agreed Henry.

83
00:04:33.809 --> 00:04:36.070
"Let's go see what Cole thinks."

84
00:04:37.651 --> 00:04:39.812
Cole was putting a frog into one of the buckets.

85
00:04:41.072 --> 00:04:43.853
Henry and Maggie hurried to Cole before he could swim away.

86
00:04:45.654 --> 00:04:47.155
Henry bent down to talk to him.

87
00:04:47.175 --> 00:04:49.596
"We were just talking to Lauren.

88
00:04:51.052 --> 00:04:52.713
We think she might still be mad at you."

89
00:04:52.733 --> 00:04:59.375
"That makes her our top suspect for everything, including dumping the frogs again," Maggie added.

90
00:04:59.395 --> 00:05:03.737
"Especially since she was the one who spotted your flip-flops."

91
00:05:04.878 --> 00:05:05.778
Cole shook his head.

92
00:05:05.798 --> 00:05:09.700
"She might have done the earlier stuff," he said.

93
00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:12.461
"But I know she didn't tip over the buckets."

94
00:05:13.781 --> 00:05:15.082
"How can you be so sure?"

95
00:05:15.442 --> 00:05:16.222
Henry asked.

96
00:05:17.303 --> 00:05:20.104
"She was near me the whole time we were jogging," Cole said.

97
00:05:21.236 --> 00:05:23.619
"She ran right behind me, yelling at me to go faster.

98
00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:28.744
She only slowed down to check on the others when I was almost all the way around the

99
00:05:28.784 --> 00:05:31.227
building." "Are you sure?"

100
00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:32.288
Maggie asked.

101
00:05:33.269 --> 00:05:33.890
Cole nodded.

102
00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:38.375
"Lauren's definitely still mad at me," he said with a sigh.

103
00:05:38.395 --> 00:05:43.020
"But she's definitely not the one who dumped those frogs back in the pool."
